  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has recently started investing in **Bitcoin**.\n\nHe assigns a **market risk level** RRR (from 111 to 101010), where:\n\n\n111 means the market is very safe,\n101010 means the market is very risky.\nChef will **buy Bitcoin** only if the risk level is **444 or less**.\n\nGiven the current risk level RRR, determine whether Chef should buy Bitcoin.\n\nPrint **\"YES\"** if Chef should buy, otherwise print **\"NO\"**.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains a single integer RRR — the current market risk level.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint `YES` if Chef should buy Bitcoin, Otherwise, print `NO`.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `YES`, `yEs`, `yes`, and `yeS` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤R≤101 \\leq R \\leq 101≤R≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2",
        "output": "YES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe current market risk is 222.\nSince 222 is not larger than 444, the risk is small enough, and Chef will buy Bitcoin."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4",
        "output": "YES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe current market risk is 444.\nSince 444 is not larger than 444, the risk is small enough, and Chef will buy Bitcoin."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5",
        "output": "NO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe current market risk is 555.\nSince 555 is larger than 444, the risk is too much, and Chef will not buy Bitcoin."
      }
    ]
  },
